# Web3 Wallet Manager

Lux provides safe wallet and transaction-management helpers that do not create,
import, store, or expose private keys. Use these helpers to model wallets,
normalize transaction requests, enforce signer policies, track transaction
state, and hand off signing to HD, hardware, multi-sig, or external signers.

## Wallet Records

```elixir
alias Lux.Web3.WalletManager

{:ok, wallet} =
  WalletManager.wallet_record(%{
    type: :hardware,
    address: "0x742d35Cc6634C0532925a3b844Bc454e4438f44e",
    label: "Treasury",
    chains: [1, 10],
    signer_ref: "ledger://1"
  })
```

## Transaction Requests

```elixir
{:ok, request} =
  WalletManager.transaction_request(%{
    chain_id: 1,
    from: wallet.address,
    to: "0x000000000000000000000000000000000000dEaD",
    value: "0xde0b6b3a7640000",
    data: "0x",
    nonce: 7
  })
```

## Policy Checks

```elixir
WalletManager.authorize_transaction(request, %{
  allowed_chains: [1, 10],
  max_value: 1_000_000_000_000_000_000
})
```

## Queue State

```elixir
item = WalletManager.queue_item(request, %{id: "tx-1"})
WalletManager.transition(item, :ready_to_sign)
WalletManager.transition(item, :signed, %{tx_hash: "0xabc"})
```

## Signing and Broadcast Plans

```elixir
WalletManager.signing_plan(request, wallet)

WalletManager.broadcast_plan(1, "0xsigned", %{
  idempotency_key: "broadcast-1"
})
```

## Monitoring Records

```elixir
WalletManager.balance_snapshot(%{
  wallet_id: wallet.id,
  address: wallet.address,
  chain_id: 1,
  balance: "0x10"
})

WalletManager.history_entry(%{
  tx_hash: "0xabc",
  chain_id: 1,
  from: wallet.address,
  to: "0x000000000000000000000000000000000000dEaD",
  status: :confirmed,
  block_number: 123
})
```

Keep private key operations inside dedicated signer adapters. This module only
passes signing payloads and records state.
